<Base title="About" description="What TheTravelFact publishes, who the byline is, and what this site will not become.">
  <article class="shell page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A sheet of sourced trip facts.</h1>
    <p>TheTravelFact is a destination sheet. One URL per place. The page holds a named climate station, month by month, and the practical facts a traveler looks up next: plug and voltage, which side of the road, tipping, tap water, the currency, the time zone, and a link to the official entry page.</p>
    <p>The byline is TheTravelFact Editors. The only email is <a href="mailto:contact@thetravelfact.com">contact@thetravelfact.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we will not publish</h2>
    <p>No national-park guide. Banff is here as a town climate sheet, not as a park. No Las Vegas, no shows, no nightlife district. No currency converter, no time-zone converter, no flight-time grid, no visa matrix. Entry rules are a link to the government page, dated, and not rewritten.</p>
    <p>A number without a source is left off the page and written down in the gaps log. We would rather have a blank cell than a borrowed one.</p>
    <h2>Design</h2>
    <p>The sheets are set like a station board and a printed almanac: a black masthead, one photograph, then ruled tables. Type is Barlow and Barlow Condensed, and IBM Plex Mono, each under the SIL Open Font License. Photographs are Wikimedia Commons files. The photographer and the licence are named on the sheet.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
